  "verbalization": "Lippiolidolic acid appears to have a direct target relationship with SMMC-7721, as evidenced by multiple paths that link the compound to SNU-387 and subsequently to SMMC-7721. The evidence suggests that Lippiolidolic acid acts as a modulator of SNU-387, which is a target of several compounds, including Anolobine and another complex molecule. This indicates that Lippiolidolic acid may exert its effects through a mechanism that involves the regulation of SNU-387, which in turn influences SMMC-7721. The presence of multiple pathways converging on SNU-387 and ending in SMMC-7721 supports the hypothesis that Lippiolidolic acid may interact with SMMC-7721 via a shared target, potentially through a common pathway or a different mechanism. The integration of these findings suggests a possible role for Lippiolidolic acid in modulating cellular processes that are relevant to SMMC-7721, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
